%N A398898 A heap of stones can be split into two heaps of equal size, possibly with an extra stone added to one of the heaps. Starting from a heap of 3*n stones, define a(n) to be the fewest  splittings needed so the heaps can be recombined into three exactly equal pieces.
%C A398898 As the growth rate appears logarithmic, this sequence might be called "bumps on a log".
%e A398898 a(3) = 4 because there is no shorter path than (9)->(4,5)->(2,2,5)->(2,2,2,3)->(1,1,2,2,3) which is partitioned into (1,2)x2 and (3) each summing to 3
%o A398898 (Python)
%o A398898 """f(n): fewest splittings of a heap of 3n stones (h -> floor(h/2), ceil(h/2))
%o A398898 so the heaps can be grouped into three parts each summing to n.
%o A398898 Structure:
%o A398898   can3(heaps, n) - subset-sum DP over pairs (sum1, sum2); third group is implied.
%o A398898   f(n)           - BFS by depth over sorted tuples (multisets) of heap sizes.
%o A398898 From Claude.ai but reads right.
%o A398898 """
%o A398898 def can3(heaps, n):
%o A398898     S = {(0, 0)}
%o A398898     for h in heaps:
%o A398898         T = set()
%o A398898         for a, b in S:
%o A398898             T.add((a, b))
%o A398898             if a + h <= n:
%o A398898                 T.add((a + h, b))
%o A398898             if b + h <= n:
%o A398898                 T.add((a, b + h))
%o A398898         S = T
%o A398898     return (n, n) in S
%o A398898 def f(n):
%o A398898     frontier = {(3 * n,)}
%o A398898     k = 0
%o A398898     while True:
%o A398898         if any(can3(s, n) for s in frontier):
%o A398898             return k
%o A398898         nxt = set()
%o A398898         for s in frontier:
%o A398898             for i, h in enumerate(s):
%o A398898                 if h > 1 and (i == 0 or s[i - 1] != h):  # skip duplicate sizes
%o A398898                     t = list(s[:i] + s[i + 1:]) + [h // 2, h - h // 2]
%o A398898                     nxt.add(tuple(sorted(t)))
%o A398898         frontier = nxt
%o A398898         k += 1
%o A398898 print([a(n) for n in range(1,10)])
%K A398898 nonn,new
%O A398898 1,1
%A A398898 _Chaim Goodman-Strauss_, Sep 27 2026
